WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:07.900
Politicians can ignore protests. They can ignore polls. They can ignore reality for surprisingly long periods (see: climate

2
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:15.500
change, nineteen seventy to present). They cannot ignore two hundred and eighty million cryptographically verified humans

3
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:21.880
saying "do this thing or we vote you out.". Not because they care about those humans.

4
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:26.380
Because they can count. What You're Actually Building. The Goal.

5
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:33.120
A website where people say "please stop letting me die of stupid things" in a way that lawyers find convincing.

6
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:40.720
On Wishonia, we would not need a website for this. We would say "please stop letting me die of stupid things" and then someone

7
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:48.420
would stop letting us die of stupid things. On your planet, this requires cryptographic verification, because your species

8
00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:52.460
lies about everything, including whether it wants to be alive.

9
00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:57.780
You need mathematical proof that people prefer living. Think about that sentence for a moment.

10
00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:03.770
You have built a civilization where "I don't want to die" requires a receipt.

11
00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:10.080
Requirements: The votes have to be real (auditable). The votes have to be secret (privacy-preserving).

12
00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:17.620
The system has to work for everyone including people without bank accounts or government I.D.s (which is most of Earth,

13
00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:24.280
a fact that surprises the people with bank accounts). The code has to be open-source so anyone can audit it.

14
00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:30.880
And the whole thing has to grow fast enough to matter before your species gets distracted by a new television show.

15
00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:39.440
Target: three point five percent global participation (two hundred and eighty million plus verified votes).

16
00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:44.260
That number isn't arbitrary. It's the number at which politicians start losing sleep.

17
00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:51.660
More on that later. The Voting System. The system uses end-to-end verifiable cryptography.

18
00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:56.220
Each voter gets a receipt that proves they voted, without proving how they voted.

19
00:01:57.020 --> 00:02:02.860
This is called a "zero-knowledge proof," which sounds like something a philosophy student made up during an exam they didn't

20
00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:08.479
study for, but it's real mathematics, and it works, and politicians cannot argue with it.

21
00:02:09.199 --> 00:02:16.500
Several have tried. The math won every time. Math is undefeated against politicians, which is the only undefeated record

22
00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:21.020
in your species' history. Every ballot published anonymized.

23
00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:25.340
Biometric data never leaves your device. All code open-source.

24
00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:31.620
The system is designed so that even the people running it can't see how you voted, which makes it more private than your

25
00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:38.220
actual elections, where the voting booth has a curtain that stops two feet off the ground and the poll worker is definitely

26
00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:46.540
looking at your shoes. On Stopping People from Cheating. Your species has been cheating at democracy since you invented

27
00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:51.060
it. The Athenians had ballot-stuffing. The Romans had vote-buying.

28
00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:57.320
Americans have gerrymandering, which is the practice of drawing voting districts in shapes that look like someone dropped

29
00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:00.520
a plate of spaghetti on a map and then legally required it.

30
00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:06.440
Three verification layers. Because one has never been enough for you.

31
00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:13.440
Layer one is the bouncer at the door. Email and phone verification, device fingerprinting, I.P.

32
00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:21.560
geolocation. Stops about ninety percent of fraud, which is the lazy fraud, which is most fraud, because cheating, like everything

33
00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:28.580
else your species does, follows a power law where most of the cheating is done by amateurs who give up if you ask them to

34
00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:32.860
verify their phone number. This is the "are you a human" layer.

35
00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:39.440
The bar is low. The fact that it catches ninety percent of attempts tells you something about the sophistication of your

36
00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:45.360
average cheater. Layer two is the V.I.P. section. Government e-I.D.

37
00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:51.560
integration (Estonia, India's Aadhaar, E.U. eIDAS, U.S. via I.D.

38
00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:58.660
dot me), biometric liveness detection (blink at the camera to prove you're not a photograph, which is a sentence that would

39
00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:06.960
confuse every human who lived before twenty ten), and proof-of-uniqueness partners like Worldcoin, BrightID, and Gitcoin

40
00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:16.079
Passport. Higher trust, higher rewards. This is the "are you a specific human who hasn't already voted as a different specific

41
00:04:16.079 --> 00:04:23.720
human" layer. Layer three is for the billions of humans who don't exist in any database because their governments can't

42
00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:29.480
be bothered to write down that they're alive. Community attestation: your neighbors confirm you're real.

43
00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:36.440
This works because lying to a computer is easy but lying to a room full of people who watched you eat breakfast is hard.

44
00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:43.430
Even Layer one gets you counted. You don't need a passport to say "I would prefer not to die."

45
00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:50.010
A.I. fraud detection: over ninety-nine percent detection, under one percent false positives.

46
00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:54.700
Biometric data stays on your device, encrypted with keys you control.

47
00:04:55.280 --> 00:05:01.180
Compliant with G.D.P.R., C.C.P.A. slash C.P.R.A., BIPA, and COPPA.

48
00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:08.780
Four different laws from four different places that all say "don't be creepy with people's data" using four different definitions

49
00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:13.820
of "creepy" and four different penalty structures for being creepy in the wrong jurisdiction.

50
00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:21.580
Your species regulates privacy the way it does everything: redundantly, inconsistently, and with great confidence.

51
00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:28.720
Growth Strategy. Your species downloaded TikTok over four billion times to watch strangers twerk.

52
00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:34.620
Getting two hundred and eighty million to click "yes" on not dying should be easier.

53
00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:43.260
It isn't, because not dying is less entertaining than twerking, but it should be, and that gap between "should be" and "isn't"

54
00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:50.860
is the entire marketing problem. Each person who signs up gets a small referral bonus for bringing the next, funded by Incentive

55
00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:55.240
Alignment Bonds. Target: less than one dollar per verified participant.

56
00:05:55.760 --> 00:06:00.760
For comparison, acquiring a coffee customer costs five to fifteen dollars.

57
00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:04.860
Nike pays forty dollars to get one person to buy shoes online.

58
00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:10.020
You're trying to convince someone to support not dying for less than the cost of a packet of gum.

59
00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:17.320
The fact that "not dying" needs a financial incentive to compete with shoes tells you everything about your species that

60
00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:21.880
this manual has been trying to tell you. But here we are. Gum money it is.

61
00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:31.560
Integrity (Proving You Didn't Cheat). Your species accuses people of cheating at everything, including children's football,

62
00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:38.820
baking competitions, and board games at Thanksgiving. The Thanksgiving ones start wars that last longer than the actual

63
00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:47.200
wars in your history books. A global referendum with actual stakes will face accusations that make your election audits

64
00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:55.740
look like casual suggestions. The defense: make cheating mathematically impossible, then publish the math.

65
00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:02.340
N.G.O. and academic observers get read-only dashboards with real-time fraud detection.

66
00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:07.470
You can't argue with a zero-knowledge proof. You can argue with a person.

67
00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:14.060
You can argue with a committee. You can't argue with math. Math doesn't have feelings.

68
00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:22.780
Math doesn't have an election coming up. Math just sits there being correct, which makes it the only trustworthy participant

69
00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:29.380
in your democratic process. Participants complete structured learning paths before voting.

70
00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:38.360
Higher reward tiers unlock as you learn more. This produces informed participants instead of confused button-clickers, though

71
00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:42.180
confused button-clickers who want to not die are also welcome.

72
00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:50.700
An uninformed person who clicks "don't let me die" is still more useful than an informed person who clicks nothing, and

73
00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:54.560
your planet has a surplus of informed people clicking nothing.

74
00:07:55.020 --> 00:08:03.440
You call them "academics." Legal positioning: non-binding global consultation with country-specific bridges to official

75
00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:12.160
mechanisms where feasible. "Non-binding" sounds weak until you remember that every major social change in your history started

76
00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:16.640
as non-binding. The suffragettes' petitions were non-binding.

77
00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:24.180
So were the civil rights marches. So was the Declaration of Independence, technically, until enough people with guns agreed

78
00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:30.660
with it. "Non-binding" is what your politicians call something before they're forced to bind to it.

79
00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:39.320
Implementation Roadmap. The realistic target for three point five percent participation (two hundred and eighty million

80
00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:48.600
verified humans) is eighteen to thirty-six months, scaling alongside the full campaign roadmap (roadmap dot Q.M.D.).

